  "title": "Felt Uncertainty Theory",
  "role": "model",
  "summary": "Mark Solms's theory, formalized with Karl Friston: the elemental form of consciousness is affect, generated in the upper brainstem as an extended form of homeostasis. Affect is felt uncertainty, the precision a self-organizing system gives its own homeostatic prediction errors, and cortex lends perception and thought their consciousness by binding that feeling.",
